        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): approval UX overhaul — inline cards, fair queue, shortcuts, badges",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nPending exec/plugin approvals are easy to miss and slow to act on: the global modal shows only the newest request (starving older ones toward their 30-minute expiry), there is no in-conversation approval surface, no per-agent/per-session indicators, no expiry visibility, and no keyboard path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nFleet operators supervising multiple agents need approvals to be scannable and fast to decide without losing safety. Queue becomes oldest-first with a selectable list; the active chat session renders its approval inline between transcript and composer (suppressed from the modal); Ctrl/Cmd chord shortcuts (Ctrl/Cmd+Enter allow once, +Shift always, +D deny) with auto-repeat guards; live mm:ss expiry countdown; per-agent count pills and per-session warning badges in the sidebar. Errors are scoped per approval id so one request's failure never hides another's. The displayed card is pinned so late-arriving requests cannot swap the command under the user's cursor.\n\n## User Impact\nApprovals surface where the user is working, oldest requests stop starving, fleet state is visible per agent/session, and keyboard users get a safe fast path. No gateway or protocol changes; UI-only.\n\n## Evidence\n- Focused suites green: ui/src/app/exec-approval.test.ts, ui/src/components/exec-approval.test.ts, ui/src/app/overlays.test.ts, ui/src/app/approval-presentation.test.ts, ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts (238 tests).\n- Remote check-changed (typecheck/lint/format shards) green on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- Structured autoreview: clean, no actionable findings (5 rounds; shortcut design hardened to modifier chords, per-request error map, pinned selection).\n",
